The strongest objection to “A is cheap” is arithmetic: the later design calls for about 160 evaluation dates out of only 166 TRAIN dates. Strict separation would leave at most six training dates before exclusions or an added embargo. The model evidence also points away from literal date memorisation as the main concern; repeated local configurations and changes in the geometry and load distribution are more plausible risks.
